      "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\nStop non-streaming `/v1/messages` from failing when a tool call's arguments aren't a JSON object, e.g. a call cut off at `max_tokens`. Part of #48273.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- Truncated, invalid or non-object arguments now become `input: {}` with a warning, instead of an HTTP 500.\r\n- Empty arguments become `{}` without a warning.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npytest -v tests/entrypoints/anthropic/test_anthropic_messages_conversion.py\r\n```\r\n\r\n129 passed. Without the fix the 6 new cases fail: `\"\"` and truncated JSON raise `JSONDecodeError`, `[...]`, `42` and `true` fail pydantic validation of the content block, and `null` comes back as `input: null`. pre-commit passes on both files. CPU only, no model needed; not tested against a running server.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n`messages_full_converter` calls `json.loads(tool_call.function.arguments)` without a guard, but tool parsers don't guarantee valid JSON there (`deepseekv31_tool_parser` passes a raw regex match through). The OpenAI route forwards `arguments` as a string, so only the Anthropic route has to decode it. Falling back to `{}` keeps the rest of the response. The warning logs the tool call id and name but not the arguments, which can contain prompt text.\r\n\r\n#52519 makes the same change to the converter, together with an unrelated realtime STT fix. This PR maps non-object JSON to `{}` rather than `{\"value\": ...}`, which isn't part of the tool's schema. Happy to close this one if you'd rather go with #52519.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n",
